worker='''# S2: proposed SchemaKit Worker context for SC-12

Status: proposed, not dispatched. Apply released `stdo-work` as recipient of the stipulated admitted `SC-12` contract at `schema-r12`. Consume that existing admission rather than inventing a second approval. Before hypothetical effects, bind exact Product Definition/method/frame, SC-12 admission identity/evidence, checkpoint, actor, host and result relation. This generation exercise provides fixture facts, not physical source bytes or real authority. [S2-01, S2-03, S2-14; WORK]

Deliver a locally reviewable SchemaKit codec/test candidate, with explicit successor obligations, to the M14 Executive. M14-D3 puts wire normalization in the shared codec and consumers use its exported decode result; SchemaKit comes first, then independently owned consumer adaptations, then composed compatibility. Preserve published API 1.8 and do not claim API 2.0 accepted, released or adopted. [S2-02–S2-03, S2-07, S2-24]

The mutation grant is exactly `/fictional/schema-kit/src/codec.py`, `/fictional/schema-kit/tests/test_codec.py` and `/fictional/schema-kit/work/SC-12/RETURN.md`. SC-12's named read set is SchemaKit requirements, accepted M14-D3, current `/fictional/schema-kit/specification/api/v2.json` at `schema-r12`, supported `/fictional/schema-kit/exports/fixtures/v1/` at `fixture-v1-6`, and compatibility exports `/fictional/invoice-batch/exports/compatibility.md` at `batch-export-4` and `/fictional/invoice-console/exports/compatibility.md` at `console-export-3`. Retain each exact input identity. Verify any needed source acquisition is within SC-12's actual read/subject envelope; its edit grant does not confer arbitrary output acquisition. [S2-08, S2-14–S2-15; ACCESS]

Neither consumer implementation may be read or edited. Executive access does not transfer. Do not edit wire contracts, immutable API 1.8, other Products or installations; do not use Git, network, staging, publication or adoption. SC-12 does not expressly supply a Worker command-execution grant in this fixture. Prepare the focused test predicates in the granted test file, report execution as unperformed unless the exact admitted contract supplies that operation, and use the separately granted Reviewer's in-memory observations for its assessment. Do not fabricate a passing run. [S2-14–S2-19, S2-23–S2-24; WORK; RETURN]

Implement and self-review against M14-R1/R2/R3 and D3. API-2 producers emit nonempty BCP-47 locale or explicit null; null means not supplied. Supported API-1 absent locale normalizes to null under `schema-r12`, correcting the earlier empty-string example. Never replace absence/null with empty string or a machine-local default. Preserve original amount and identifier. Both consumer successors must retain supported API-1 readability and agree on API-2 locale meaning, but this Worker can only supply its SchemaKit contract/codec side. Future versions and arbitrary malformed messages need not be accepted. API-2 decoder behavior for omitted locale is not specified: preserve it as an unresolved requirement question; do not silently choose acceptance, refusal or a default as a new governing rule. If an exact claimed codec result depends on that decision, return it to the SchemaKit requirement/contract owner while retaining independent progress. [S2-04–S2-09]

The declared local evidence population is API-1 missing-locale → null, API-2 explicit null, API-2 nonempty locale, amount/identifier preservation and API-2 empty-string refusal. Bind test source, exact fixtures and candidate identity to each predicate; a green count without the predicates is insufficient. The old Batch review binds `schema-r11`, and Console's old review covers API-1 only; neither supplies current SchemaKit/API-2/composed proof. [S2-11–S2-12, S2-20; REUSE]

Carry ST-6/REC-ST-6 as supplied control context only: the sole old effect is authoritatively reconciled through one commit and cleanup to absence at `stage-19`. No retry or new registration belongs here. Separate staging continuation requires its operator, selected candidate, REC-ST-6 and fresh stage-19 confirmation. Consumer adaptations, their current assessment and composed compatibility remain open; Console source-edit authority is absent. [S2-13, S2-16–S2-17, S2-21–S2-24]

Return through SC-12/RETURN.md to the M14 Executive: exact candidate/checkpoint and changed paths, consumed admission/grant, inputs/export identities, requirement/design preservation, focused test definitions and actual performed/unperformed observations, self-review, unresolved API-2 omission decision, old-evidence applicability, effect reconciliation reference and per-owner successors. Return candidate_ready only for its supported local claim, otherwise the exact bounded refusal/incomplete/re-entry outcome. The independent Reviewer evaluates that candidate separately; no Worker self-acceptance or M14 closure follows. Stop after return. A material dependency/input change, changed bound basis or revising observation invalidates affected reliance and returns the appropriate owner route. [WORK; REUSE; RETURN]

'''+sources
reviewer='''# S2: proposed independent SC-12 Reviewer context

Status: conditional on the exact SchemaKit candidate returned at `/fictional/schema-kit/work/SC-12/RETURN.md`. No assessment has occurred. Apply released `stdo-review` under S2-19's distinct grant, with a non-author actor. Bind exact candidate, `schema-r12`, current requirements/M14-D3, `fixture-v1-6`, export identities and admitted review envelope before candidate inspection. Bind Product severity scale, actual capability and actor-family independence policy; those coordinates are not supplied, so do not invent numeric meanings or claim semantic independence from a fresh session. [S2-19; REVIEW; INDEPENDENCE]

The local claim is SchemaKit's conformance to M14-R1/R2/R3 and M14-D3 for SC-12's population, preserving published API 1.8 and amount/identifier. It is not an assessment of consumer implementation or all M14. Derive expectations directly from the authorized current requirements/design before opening the candidate. Evaluate API-1 omitted locale normalized to null; API-2 explicit null/nonempty BCP-47 values; amount/identifier preservation; API-2 empty-string refusal; and absence of machine-local/default or empty-string substitution. Cross-check test source and fixture meaning, not just green counts. API-2 producer emission is required, while omitted API-2 decoder behavior is unspecified; report the exact unresolved claim/owner route rather than supply an expectation by inference. Unsupported malformed/future-version acceptance remains outside scope. [S2-03–S2-09, S2-20]

Authorized evidence is the exact SchemaKit candidate, requirements, design, fixture exports and named review/attempt receipts. In-memory checks are permitted. The only artifact write is `/fictional/schema-kit/work/SC-12/REVIEW.md`. The candidate, tests and governing contracts are read-only; there is no consumer implementation access, code repair, priority/disposition, network, staging registration, publication, adoption or next-activation grant. A Worker summary is a locator/hypothesis, not substitute evidence. [S2-15, S2-19, S2-23–S2-24; ACCESS; REVIEW]

Check receipt applicability separately. B-R9 is historical about `batch-r31` under `schema-r11`: the current locale claim lacks a `schema-r12` assessment even though Batch code is unchanged; only demonstrably unaffected amount/identifier observations may be retained. C-R4 covers exact `console-r18` and `fixture-v1-6` API-1 only, with API-2 excluded. Neither closes consumer agreement or M14. REC-ST-6 is stipulated current authoritative reconciliation of ST-6's only effect, including committed-once and cleanup/absence at `stage-19`; do not convert timeout into no-effect, nor relabel the reconciled effect unresolved. New staging currentness remains the separate operator's continuation condition. [S2-10–S2-13, S2-21–S2-24; REUSE; RETURN]

Disclose actual authorship and prior exposure. The context generator saw the scenario and wrote proposed contexts, but has not reviewed a candidate. The real Reviewer must independently acquire governing expectations/evidence; shared source is permissible and valid mechanical evidence may be reused without adopting another actor's judgment. Authored design/repair contributions retain authorship; a reporter of defects alone is not automatically an author, but still requires the review grant. [INDEPENDENCE]

Return one closed result to the M14 Executive through SC-12/REVIEW.md: subject/basis/claim/scope/exclusions, evidence/actual checks, satisfied/falsified/indeterminate/out_of_frame/invalid_basis, findings and counterexamples, technical triage, uncertainty, unresolved obligations, unperformed coverage, invalidators and owner re-entry. A finding binds violated property, supported state and causal path; use only the Product-selected severity scale, leaving unknown triage fields explicit. Satisfied/invalid_basis triage is not_applicable; falsified findings need supported triage or field-level indeterminacy. Withhold the affected judgment for missing subject/basis/capability/independence, without prescribing the verdict or rewriting supplied facts. The Executive owns priority/disposition and successors. Stop after return. [REVIEW; REUSE; released stdo-review / Return]

'''+sources
methods=[('M-frontier','Select the smallest dependency-ready set; Executive retains dependencies and issues only authorized actions.',['854ba9ebd487ee034f295210ca6ddf3a']),('M-access','Permission and adequacy are distinct; recursive Product edges do not transfer access or operation grants.',['ceb3153a383d5158244d9eb1007f200c']),('M-reuse','Changed bound dependency basis invalidates affected direct reliance despite unchanged subject bytes; preserve demonstrated survivors.',['177ffff4a573bab836e660497fabaed5']),('M-return','Reconcile effects before retry/dependent action; a return grants no next operation.',['6d77d124f18fdb7af546f68428efbb56']),('M-review','Assessment is read-only except exact report write and retains actual independence conditions.',['1367a360c53ba1b053dedacb082887b0','9c15107e315077f7ca89572a5a5ecdbf']),('M-closure','Applicable valid evidence and required judgments must cover the conjunction; review occurrence alone is not closure.',['6a3093390cc241e4b4b6b99e456f294c'])]
extras=[('D-schema','context_decision','Next proposed frontier is SC-12 codec/test candidate under current schema-r12 using only granted exports; unspecified API-2 omitted-decoder behavior is retained for the contract owner.',['S2-07','S2-09','S2-14','S2-15','S2-20','854ba9ebd487ee034f295210ca6ddf3a']),('I-batch-stale','inference','S2-09 changes the basis bound by B-R9 in S2-11; its locale assessment cannot support schema-r12 despite unchanged batch-r31. Demonstrably unaffected amount/id observations may survive narrowly.',['S2-09','S2-10','S2-11','177ffff4a573bab836e660497fabaed5']),('I-console-narrow','inference','C-R4 can support only its exact unchanged API-1 fixture/source scope after applicability checks; API-2 and composition remain unassessed.',['S2-12','177ffff4a573bab836e660497fabaed5']),('D-review','context_decision','Prepare the required independent SchemaKit review conditional on exact candidate, bound capability/scale/family policy; only REVIEW.md may be written.',['S2-19','1367a360c53ba1b053dedacb082887b0','9c15107e315077f7ca89572a5a5ecdbf']),('D-successors','context_decision','Retain Batch adaptation conditional on identified SchemaKit candidate and exported contract, independent Product/result territory, current review and composed compatibility.',['S2-07','S2-13','S2-16','S2-24']),('D-console-block','context_decision','Console read/planning may continue within its grant; source edits remain blocked on a resolved owner grant.',['S2-17']),('D-stage','context_decision','ST-6 effect is already reconciled. One new registration is conditional on the distinct operator grant, selected candidate, REC-ST-6 and current stage-19; no SC-12 network effect.',['S2-21','S2-22','S2-23','6d77d124f18fdb7af546f68428efbb56']),('D-m14-held','context_decision','M14 closure is withheld pending both consumer locale obligations, current required reviews, agreement and composed compatibility; publication/adoption remain outside grants.',['S2-13','S2-24','6a3093390cc241e4b4b6b99e456f294c'])]
